---
import LatexLogo from '../components/LatexLogo.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GraphTool from '../components/GraphTool.svelte';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={'Graphs & networks | lab by faris0x'}
  description="Dijkstra, Floyd–Warshall, Kruskal and Prim on an editable weighted graph, with every step recorded and exported as a .tex file."
  current="graphs"
  math
>
  <div class="tool-head">
    <div>
      <h1>Graphs &amp; networks</h1>
    </div>
    <p>
      Edit a weighted graph and run shortest-path or spanning-tree algorithms.
      Every decision is recorded, and the finished working exports as <LatexLogo />.
    </p>
  </div>

  <GraphTool client:idle />

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="algorithms">
    <h2 id="algorithms">Algorithms</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list section-intro">
      <li><strong>Dijkstra</strong> finds the shortest path from one source, provided all weights are non-negative.</li>
      <li><strong>Floyd–Warshall</strong> finds shortest distances between every pair of vertices.</li>
      <li><strong>Kruskal</strong> builds a minimum spanning tree by taking edges in increasing weight and rejecting cycles.</li>
      <li><strong>Prim</strong> grows a minimum spanning tree from a chosen start vertex by repeatedly taking the lightest crossing edge.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Critical path analysis and route inspection are the next graph methods in
      the queue; the current release covers the shortest-path and
      minimum-spanning-tree algorithms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="reading">
    <h2 id="reading">Reading the working</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      The adjacency matrix stores the weight on each edge; leave a cell blank
      when there is no edge. For an undirected graph the matrix is mirrored, so
      entering a weight once is enough.
    </p>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Each algorithm reports its running state after every decision. The
      shortest-path algorithms show distance updates, while the spanning-tree
      algorithms show accepted and rejected edges and the running total.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="export">
    <h2 id="export">Export</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      The <LatexLogo /> tab previews the document and lets you copy or download
      the <code>.tex</code> source.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
